{
    desc => q{3u undoes 3 changes at once},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/undo_count_3u`

Tests that **3u** undoes 3 separate change operations in a single command.
Three separate `dd` commands are performed, then `3u` reverts all three at once.

**Keys:** `dd`, `dd`, `dd`, `3u`

**initial.png**
- Buffer has 3 lines: "one", "two", "three"
- Cursor on line 1

**after_3dd.png**
- Buffer has 0 lines (all three lines deleted one by one)
- Intermediate snapshot showing all changes applied

**after_3u.png**
- Buffer restored to 3 lines (identical to initial)
- All three undo steps applied at once via 3u
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('dd');
        $ctx->delay(50);
        $ctx->keys('dd');
        $ctx->delay(50);
        $ctx->keys('dd');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_3dd');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('3u');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_3u');
    },
}
__DATA__
one
two
three
